  "research_findings": [
    "Race freedom alone does not prove safe storage reuse: A.write\u2192B.write\u2192A.read is ordered but overlapping storage destroys a live A value.",
    "Partial value lifetimes plus completion and overwrite facts enable a concrete allocation optimization even while another part of A remains live.",
    "The corresponding memory-generation change must remain visible to ordinary compiler optimizations; otherwise CSE can incorrectly reuse a stale load."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Experimental opt-in recognizer; one placement per two-partition straightline WS region",
    "No loop generations, dynamic phases, conditional control flow, arbitrary layouts/dtypes, scaled MMA, or multiCTA inference",
    "Does not synthesize synchronization or automatically recreate the complete looping two-CTA Gluon06 overlap algorithm",
    "Captured attention, persistent attention, GEMM and original overlap IR are unchanged by the new pass; no unmodified real-kernel speedup established",
    "Finite models, source audit and sampled GPU runs are not a general hardware correctness proof",
